Cry out, Song of Willow!

265
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:27,860
Oh, my God.

266
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,360
Oh, my God.

267
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:15,697
I got no idea what kind of
chunk is waiting for me.

268
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:18,839
As soon as I get back up,
I better get me some cola.

269
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:19,950
All right.

270
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:23,004
I wonder if that deer is
still hanging in there.

271
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:27,031
What's going on up there?

272
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:42,720
What the hell is that?

273
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:52,180
Wait, that's the CP9 guy that
got locked in the fridge.

274
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:55,593
That thing's holding him like a ragdoll.

275
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,820
What the hell did I miss?

276
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,760
That hat!

277
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,941
I think it's the same style
that deer was wearing!

278
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:17,220
Hey, you!

279
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:19,698
You're not that deer gorilla, right?

280
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:36,620
This can't be real.

281
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,980
No, it's him, all right.

282
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,160
It's Kumadori.

283
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:45,680
His body came rocketing
over from the Tower of Law.

284
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,078
But who could have done that to him?

285
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:53,732
Seriously, what the hell is this problem?

286
00:20:08,820 --> 00:20:09,820
A voice?

287
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:17,200
Hey, keep moving.

288
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:20,561
I don't remember telling
you to stop, Nico Robin.

289
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:23,600
Hey, are you listening to me?

290
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:25,801
Don't forget who's the boss here.

291
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,220
All right, Luchi.

292
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:28,580
Just drag her.

293
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,918
Pull her by the hair if you have to.

294
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:35,740
It's an order.

295
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,400
Now come on.

296
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:38,580
Start walking.

297
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,260
You're delusional, aren't you? Oh my.

298
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:48,897
You're honestly convinced that the Straw
Hats are still on their way to rescue you.

299
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:54,160
I've never seen such a
weak-looking pirate crew.

300
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:56,977
If that's your only
hope, that's pretty sad.

301
00:20:57,060 --> 00:21:00,557
That explosion we heard earlier was
probably the pipes or something.

302
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,857
There's no way they
could make it this far.

303
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:06,417
While you're up in your little fantasy
world dreaming of being rescued,

304
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,382
we'll pass the Gates of Justice.

305
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:12,920
The Bridge of Hesitation lies
right before the Gates of Justice.

306
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:15,877
We'll cross the first
elevated half of the bridge,

307
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:18,277
and once the gates are within our sight,

308
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:21,420
The other half of the bridge
will rise from the sea,

309
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:24,893
and then we'll finally pass
through the gates themselves.

310
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:30,162
Once the gates are firmly closed behind
us, every lingering trace of your pathetic,

311
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:32,928
misguided optimism will
be dashed to pieces.

312
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:35,537
You'll forget what hope even means.

313
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:38,017
The only feeling left in your body will be

314
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:40,629
an overwhelming and
eternal sense of guilt.

315
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:45,661
You will spend your days in ceaseless
atonement for your arrogant crime of existing.

316
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:48,740
You know it's true, Nico. Robin.

317
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:11,160
Now then, hurry along.

318
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,240
Move your feet, wench.

319
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:23,060
ROBIN! ROBIN!

320
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:36,060
What was that?

321
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:37,320
I heard someone!

322
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:38,410
Did you hear that?

323
00:22:38,493 --> 00:22:39,323
Who was it?

324
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:44,917
You better take Nico
Robin and start moving.

325
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,037
Don't worry, Chief.

326
00:22:46,120 --> 00:22:47,120
I'll handle this.

327
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:50,740
The door!

328
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:55,192
At least it doesn't look like
it's made of iron this time!

329
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:08,600
It's big in here!

330
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:09,780
Where am I?

331
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:15,000
I found you, pigeon bastard!

332
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:19,940
Glad you could make it.
